  "agent": {
    "note": "master — @m0saic/alpine/treemap/v1 (the 9th + FINAL Alpine template, completing the pack), LOCKED 2026-06-23. A squarified treemap in the friendly white card: value-sized rounded tiles packed to fill the card (Bruls/Huizing/van Wijk squarify → balanced aspect ratios, no slivers), each labelled top-left with its name + share, tiles fading in biggest→smallest. Built on the donut/heatmap absolute-placement model (tight rects on the 4px lattice, grid as a full-canvas extraLayer → no quantization). Palette cycles ALPINE_PALETTE (per-item override); label contrast auto-flips (white on saturated tiles). Labels SHRINK-TO-FIT their tile and only truncate (ellipsis) when even the min font overflows; small tiles hide labels. Knobs (most human-facing): valueMode (percent/value/none), cornerRadius (0..0.5 slider), showValue, per-item color, preset. Two label fixes in the sandbox: shrink-to-fit (so medium tiles show full names) + a clear name→value gap with the label clearing the rounded corner at high radius. 5 stress variants approved across all 3 aspects (A dark-horizontal · B square-8 · C vertical-portrait · D value+colors+radius0.3 · E twelve-static). Shipped alongside: the render-hero rounding mirror (it now previews rounded tiles) + Make opening .mosaicx recipes as live templates.",
    "question": "Locked master — showcase props (5-dept HEADCOUNT treemap, percent labels, fade cascade). This is the preview the Templates page renders.",
    "response": {
      "body": "Approved — locked. Completes the Alpine pack.",
      "from": "human",
      "at": "2026-06-23T00:00:00.000Z"
    }
  },
